{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1097992-fighting-with-2-dot-arcana","id":1097992,"title":"Fighting with 2 dot arcana","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-05-28T22:59:18-07:00","id":1097992,"title":"Fighting with 2 dot arcana","content":"I read some post saying that with just 2 dots of arcana was enough to fight or even kill someone. Im probably lacking in imagination because i cant figure it out how.<br /> What can you do with just 2 dots?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11395-shaddar","name":"Shaddar","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"338"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-28T23:26:55-07:00","id":1097994,"title":"","content":"Here are some examples of what I use with my character (Note that most of my tactics are less-than-lethal):<br /> <br /> Mind 2- Psychic Domination to cause someone to flee, or fall asleep, or otherwise incapacitate themselves<br /> Time 2- Freeze them in place whilst you make an escape or flank them<br /> Fate 2- Curse them into utter failure with any actions taken against you in combat<br /> Space 2-Isolate them from everything in their vicinity( this is done with Space 1. Nasty little spell)<br /> <br /> There are others ways to deal with someone in a lethal manner, but direct damage eludes you at this level. Instead, you can only supplement attacks against someone, through obfuscation, protection, or cleverly using spells originally intended for something else. The classic &quot;Shielding them from any and all oxygen entering their area&quot; is a particularly neat tactic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8573-zombiecakes","name":"Zombiecakes","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"213"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-29T00:08:24-07:00","id":1098009,"title":"","content":"Forces 2 is enough to create a gravity funnel/tunnel.<br /> The possibilities are endless.<br /> <br /> Also the Kinetic Blow spell is incredible if you want to fight &quot;normally&quot; but with an edge.<br /> You can also use the Reach options to get some truly impressive results.<br /> Stunning/Knock-Down playing card thrown weapons that deal as much Lethal damage as a shotgun, for all of your Gambit needs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12644,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12644-herbertisbestbert","user":"HerbertIsBestBert","date":". 05-29-2017, 06:53 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12644-herbertisbestbert","name":"HerbertIsBestBert","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12644_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"312"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-29T01:36:58-07:00","id":1098023,"title":"","content":"A few more examples.<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Making yourself invisible/undetectable using Mind/Forces/Prime or Life and then attacking using mundane weapons works pretty well.</li> <li>Forces and Matter both have 2 dot spells that can vastly increase the lethality of those weapons too.</li> <li>1 dot of Matter lets you Remote Control machines, including things like nearby cars, which can be directed to smash into your opponents.</li> <li>Control Electricity (2 dot of forces) lets you zap someone with nearby power sources for considerable Bashing Damage, Control Fire can also be used as a lethal weapon if a fire already exists nearby.</li> </ol>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6230-katana1515","name":"Katana1515","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6230_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"280"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-29T03:15:51-07:00","id":1098044,"title":"","content":"Matters Craftsman Eye for 1 dot is pretty good, giving weapons 8 again by just examining it for a turn is awesome. (it actually makes &quot;Find the Balance&quot; at 2 dots subpar)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-29T05:10:29-07:00","id":1098069,"title":"","content":"You're a Gnosis 1 Apprentice of Mind. You have the Shadow Name merit at 3 dots and Psychic Domination as a Praxis.<br /> <br /> You cast Psychic Domination on your rival with the Command &quot;Kill Yourself Immediately&quot;.<br /> <br /> You require 1 reach to make the spell instant cast, 1 reach to cast at sensory range and 2 reach to let you issue a suicidal command.<br /> <br /> Your dice pool starts at 3. You use your Persona as a Yantra to boost the pool to 6. You chant in the High Speech boosting your pool to 8. Willpower gets you to 11.<br /> <br /> You're overreaching a fair bit, but your gnosis is nice and low so you're only taking three paradox dice. Except you're the kind of person who's built a magical persona around ordering people to kill themselves, so lets face it, its likely you've inured yourself to this spell in terms of wisdom loss, so that's another +2, bringing you to 5. You've already wasted a whole turn chanting, and don't have time to spend five rounds spending mana to drop that pool to zero. You let rip!<br /> <br /> With 11 dice you've got a &gt;70% chance of scoring the three successes you need for an exceptional success, which will allow you to bypass your target's withstand entirely and make your meager potency irrelevant.<br /> <br /> With a five dice paradox pool, you've got a &gt;80% of getting a success on your paradox roll, and a 50/50 shot of getting two. Fuck it, not your problem.<br /> <br /> You score two successes on your paradox roll. The storyteller spends both reach to change the subject of the spell.<br /> <br /> The spell goes off without a hitch and as you prepare to shoot yourself in the head, the only thought that has time to go through your mind is &quot;I probably deserve this.&quot;<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5958,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5958-logocentric","user":"Logocentric","date":". 05-29-2017, 08:27 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5958-logocentric","name":"Logocentric","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5958_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"44"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-29T06:48:08-07:00","id":1098093,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zombiecakes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1097992-fighting-with-2-dot-arcana?p=1097994#post1097994\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The classic &quot;Shielding them from any and all oxygen entering their area&quot; is a particularly neat tactic.</div> </div> </div> </div>That isn't Shielding, which is purely about protective spells. You would have to use Ruling. Same effect, different Practice.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5958-logocentric\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar5958_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"5958\" data-vbnamecard=\"5958\">Logocentric</a> If you didn't contain it then, yeah, you would.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2632,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","user":"Mrmdubois","date":". 05-29-2017, 09:51 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-29T07:17:37-07:00","id":1098097,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Logocentric</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1097992-fighting-with-2-dot-arcana?p=1098069#post1098069\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You score two successes on your paradox roll. The storyteller spends both reach to change the subject of the spell.<br /> <br /> The spell goes off without a hitch and as you prepare to shoot yourself in the head, the only thought that has time to go through your mind is &quot;I probably deserve this.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>And this, ladies and gentlemen, is why you always try to contain your Paradoxes. Not only does it stop you from accidentally shooting yourself, it stops Paradox from knocking dice off your pool and reducing your chances of that Exceptional Success you want.<br /> <br /> Consider your Paradox Condition a memento of your kill.<br /> <br /> (Also a big red flag for the Guardians to come Deal With you, but hey, that still beats already having killed yourself.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1909,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1909-juhn","user":"Juhn","date":". 05-29-2017, 10:21 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1909-juhn","name":"Juhn","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"302"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-29T07:30:23-07:00","id":1098099,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Logocentric</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1097992-fighting-with-2-dot-arcana?p=1098069#post1098069\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You score two successes on your paradox roll. The storyteller spends both reach to change the subject of the spell.</div> </div> </div> </div>Out of well over 150 spell casting rolls made in my games, I've only seen a non-scelesti choose to release it twice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-29T08:26:35-07:00","id":1098104,"title":"","content":"I did consider putting a bit about the likelyhood of a mage who's built their persona around making people commit suicide having a high enough wisdom pool to contain their paradoxes reliably into my little morality play, but the botched paradox being a consequence of our hypothetical suicide slinger's own decision seemed like the more satisfying ending to me.<br /> <br /> He is only a Gnosis 1 apprentice after all, maybe nobody's taught him how to contain paradoxes yet. There's a reason the Mysterium include that lesson as part of their basic induction process.<br /> <br /> We're well rid of him anyway. He was a bad egg.<br /> <br /> Edit: In general, it's something I really like about combat in Mage that it's full of shenanigans I Win Buttons. It's generally a safe assumption that any mage with the inclination towards that kind of thing has a strategy in place to just delete you if they win the initiative roll. I think the addition of praxes really helps cement this in 2E too as it helps promote the idea that mages have favored spells and ways of doing things. It means the way to get an edge is to figure out what particular path to single-round domination your mark favors and preparing an appropriate counter. This leads to fun &quot;I know that you know that I know&quot; mind games between longer term rivals and is generally very Mage-ish.<br /> <br /> Edit edit: It also means that combats in Mage are generally over more quickly than they might be with other splats, while still being tense and full of drama.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5958,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5958-logocentric","user":"Logocentric","date":". 05-29-2017, 11:39 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5958-logocentric","name":"Logocentric","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5958_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"44"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-29T09:02:15-07:00","id":1098114,"title":"","content":"Use Forces 2 and the Practice of Ruling to throw fire produced from a lighter at people.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-29T09:36:59-07:00","id":1098120,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aiden</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1097992-fighting-with-2-dot-arcana?p=1098114#post1098114\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Use Forces 2 and the Practice of Ruling to throw fire produced from a lighter at people.</div> </div> </div> </div>It is kind of funny / ironic that Forces, which you'd expect to the best blasty / aggro arcana is generally the least impressive when it comes to straight lethality, especially at lower levels. If your ST allows you to do it without conjunctional life the easiest instagib I've found with forces is shorting the electrical circuitry of your targets body to stop their heart from beating, but it's an edge case, and isn't exactly what you think of when it comes to forces kills anyway.<br /> <br /> Water has a critical temperature of 374 \u00b0C - if you could spontaneously raise someone's body temperature to this number you could get some fairly spectacular effects, but again this feels like something that requires conjunctional life, and even if it doesn't the rules on temperature control don't really deal with things at this level of granularity so it's very much gonna be down to your ST how much potency you need to achieve this,<br /> <br /> .","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5958-logocentric","name":"Logocentric","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5958_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"44"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-29T09:59:22-07:00","id":1098130,"title":"","content":"Life 2 works just as well as Mind 2 for getting a person to kill themselves by the way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-29T14:06:11-07:00","id":1098233,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>totalgit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1097992-fighting-with-2-dot-arcana?p=1098044#post1098044\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Matters Craftsman Eye for 1 dot is pretty good, giving weapons 8 again by just examining it for a turn is awesome. (it actually makes &quot;Find the Balance&quot; at 2 dots subpar)</div> </div> </div> </div>Much as 2e Changeling's Inanimate Communion and Blessing of Perfection can both grant roughly the same effect at different levels, the important distinction is that you can't use Craftsman's Eye on an object and then hand off the 8-Again to someone else.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-29T14:17:03-07:00","id":1098238,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Logocentric</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1097992-fighting-with-2-dot-arcana?p=1098104#post1098104\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I did consider putting a bit about the likelyhood of a mage who's built their persona around making people commit suicide having a high enough wisdom pool to contain their paradoxes reliably into my little morality play, but the botched paradox being a consequence of our hypothetical suicide slinger's own decision seemed like the more satisfying ending to me.<br /> <br /> He is only a Gnosis 1 apprentice after all, maybe nobody's taught him how to contain paradoxes yet. There's a reason the Mysterium include that lesson as part of their basic induction process.<br /> <br /> We're well rid of him anyway. He was a bad egg.</div> </div> </div> </div>I get the logic, but just as a brief rules clarification: when you roll to contain a Paradox, you still contain the Paradox <i>even if you roll absolutely no successes</i>: all that means is the resulting Paradox Condition is more severe, as none of the Paradox successes were converted into Resistant Bashing Damage instead.<br /> <br /> Of course, I can also buy that someone hubristic enough to force people to commit suicide might be hubristic enough to regularly risk death in order to not suffer the humiliation and indignity of Abyssal-Taint-Induced-Insanity (or whatever else the Paradox condition ends up being, but that seems likely enough for a Paradox on a Mind spell). After all, it's never going to <i>actually happen</i>. Until it does.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1909-juhn","name":"Juhn","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"302"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-29T15:54:13-07:00","id":1098264,"title":"","content":"From a defensive standpoint, don't forget that Forces 2 can render you effectively immune to all kinetic (and heat, electricity, etc.) damage. Frenzying vampire? Death rage werewolf? Rampaging creature of the night? Meh. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> You might not always be an unstoppable force, but it really doesn't take much to be the immovable object.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-29T19:22:13-07:00","id":1098316,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1097992-fighting-with-2-dot-arcana?p=1098099#post1098099\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Out of well over 150 spell casting rolls made in my games, I've only seen a non-scelesti choose to release it twice.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bIt's a stupid choice with little chance of upside except in rare corner cases. They completely dropped the ball with this implementation. It should be free choice up to a certain level of reach before the GM does her thing otherwise why even have it as a viable option for non Scelesti mages? Waste of ink and paper it's printed on. Luckily houserules are a thing and everyone uses them to various degrees.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2682,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2682-kumiko","user":"Kumiko","date":". 05-29-2017, 10:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2682-kumiko","name":"Kumiko","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2682_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-29T19:42:38-07:00","id":1098321,"title":"","content":"You want temptation to release or contain? Let non Scelesti mages have the ACTUAL choice to release at some level of overreach. The current binary implementation doesn't even warrant thinking about doing it. Now you give non Scelesti a free reach or two specifically usable to counter whatever the GM wants to do via twisting your spell contested via CoW....now you have choice and some dark &quot;good&quot; guys like in my game. Everyone takes risk with every spell and it hammers the point home why the other Night People are scared and don't trust mages in any situation because they're complete wildcards as they should be regardless of their personal ethics or morality. That's the downside of being a mage. Nobody but another mage understands you, not sleepers, not sleepwalkers, not proximi or Second Sight types, or other types of Night People regardless of being full or half template types.<br /> <br /> \u200bI haven't gone as far as making any overreach a Clash of Wills vs. Scelesti getting release for free but it worked for Wheel of Time with the Iron Will merit and I'm hard pressed to see why it shouldn't be the same rules for everyone but with penalties to non scelesti. We're talking about people that form imagos of what they want to happen at the soul level. That is so much deeper then willpower/wish magic beyond ridiculousness. So yeah, I figure a Clash of Wills role is appropriate before the Abyss or the GM gets to play. YMMV","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2682,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2682-kumiko","user":"Kumiko","date":". 05-29-2017, 11:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2682-kumiko","name":"Kumiko","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2682_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-29T20:22:39-07:00","id":1098331,"title":"","content":"Since my favorite are Obrimos, TK and other brute control of elements have been mentioned. What hasn't been mentioned is electronics and their utter control over them.... any drones in the area? Otherwise in combat at this level Fate, Life, Mind are all useful if not deadly. Typically I prefer Fate because I love the Awakened Gambit over the Life/Mind legacies of the Obrimos but any of those Arcanum at 2 dots are deadly especially as a praxis or inured.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2682,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2682-kumiko","user":"Kumiko","date":". 05-29-2017, 11:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2682-kumiko","name":"Kumiko","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2682_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-29T20:38:48-07:00","id":1098333,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>branford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1097992-fighting-with-2-dot-arcana?p=1098264#post1098264\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">From a defensive standpoint, don't forget that Forces 2 can render you effectively immune to all kinetic (and heat, electricity, etc.) damage. Frenzying vampire? Death rage werewolf? Rampaging creature of the night? Meh. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> You might not always be an unstoppable force, but it really doesn't take much to be the immovable object.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, going by the example of Alchemist's Touch reapplied to kinetic damage, even with Reach you can still only decrease Agg by Potency.<br /> Which in certain extreme cases, facing certin extremely motivated and competent enemies, even Shielding won't be able to save you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12644-herbertisbestbert","name":"HerbertIsBestBert","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12644_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"312"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-29T20:50:55-07:00","id":1098336,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HerbertIsBestBert</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1097992-fighting-with-2-dot-arcana?p=1098333#post1098333\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, going by the example of Alchemist's Touch reapplied to kinetic damage, even with Reach you can still only decrease Agg by Potency.<br /> Which in certain extreme cases, facing certin extremely motivated and competent enemies, even Shielding won't be able to save you.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bSo no one hit kill shot of something above your paygrade? Got it. OP SPECIFICALLY asked how to use 2 dot magic in combat. Try again given nobody can do combined spells or do direct kill shots at this level. Use a gun and Fate/Life or Forces from long range or have a Prime/Life net up and come back on your terms.<br /> <br /> I'm asking because the actual question isn't can a Mage kill anything but why they don't. They can do it easily at this level and after, if they are fighting why are they attempting to break the rules set down by the Exarchs and fight them directly. Both orders have theirs so why the reason for the Cold War? Other then the fact the Exarchs are full of shit and directly responsible for the cesspool that current reality is? Painfully obvious why anyone not a reaper joined the FC and it's more obvious why they are large and make The Diamond really large. Most people like the concept of Freedom but have no clue what it actually means.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2682,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2682-kumiko","user":"Kumiko","date":". 05-30-2017, 01:08 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2682-kumiko","name":"Kumiko","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2682_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-29T21:51:11-07:00","id":1098348,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HerbertIsBestBert</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1097992-fighting-with-2-dot-arcana?p=1098333#post1098333\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, going by the example of Alchemist's Touch reapplied to kinetic damage, even with Reach you can still only decrease Agg by Potency.<br /> Which in certain extreme cases, facing certin extremely motivated and competent enemies, even Shielding won't be able to save you.</div> </div> </div> </div>Figure what's good for the gander is good for the goose and be smart like everyone is trying to tell you. Basically If you're not an AA be indirect but pick your spots for direct action or maybe just do what any smart mage at this level does and set your actual intention up though a couple spells that set the environment in your control. Even DnD 5e wizards require the same. You are a Controller not a Blaster. Accept that your strength is mental and as a Kingmaker and chessmaster regardless of order/faction and you get the motivation of a typical mage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2682,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2682-kumiko","user":"Kumiko","date":". 05-30-2017, 01:01 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2682-kumiko","name":"Kumiko","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2682_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-30T12:07:17-07:00","id":1098508,"title":"","content":"Shouldn't you be able to cast a Ruling Life spell that basically forces target's organism into a state where it kills or greatly damages itself? Things like &quot;Rule over targets heart to make it stop beating&quot;? Physical Domination, kind of?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-30T12:36:29-07:00","id":1098514,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1097992-fighting-with-2-dot-arcana?p=1098508#post1098508\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Shouldn't you be able to cast a Ruling Life spell that basically forces target's organism into a state where it kills or greatly damages itself? Things like &amp;quot;Rule over targets heart to make it stop beating&amp;quot;? Physical Domination, kind of?</div> </div> </div> </div>Force a person's body to pick up a weapon and use it on themselves yes, force a heart attack I don't think so.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-30T13:00:32-07:00","id":1098520,"title":"","content":"I think forcing a heart to stop beating would fall under 'fundamentally altering the target's abilities'. As far as I know, there aren't living organisms today whose hearts <i>can</i> stop beating as part of their functionality.<br /> <br /> Now, using Ruling to make someone hold their breath until they die of suffocation should work fine, I think.<br /> <br /> Alternatively, one would think that you could pull of a marionette style spell (and I've designed something similar for corpses at Death 2) with just Ruling, allowing you to force the target to bodily take specific actions - such as Mrmdubois' suggestion. But Life, for some reason, has this type of effect at Life 4.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-30T13:03:44-07:00","id":1098523,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1097992-fighting-with-2-dot-arcana?p=1098508#post1098508\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Shouldn't you be able to cast a Ruling Life spell that basically forces target's organism into a state where it kills or greatly damages itself? Things like &quot;Rule over targets heart to make it stop beating&quot;? Physical Domination, kind of?</div> </div> </div> </div>Can you combine Control Heat (Forces 2) with Life 2 to cook someone alive by raising their temperature by ten grades or so?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12892-kammerer","name":"Kammerer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12892_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-30T13:06:20-07:00","id":1098524,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1097992-fighting-with-2-dot-arcana?p=1098520#post1098520\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think forcing a heart to stop beating would fall under 'fundamentally altering the target's abilities'. As far as I know, there aren't living organisms today whose hearts <i>can</i> stop beating as part of their functionality.</div> </div> </div> </div>Uh. All living organisms can do that? Heart is a muscle, and <i>not </i>contracting is pretty easy. If muscles had &quot;fundamental abilities&quot;, then &quot;contracting&quot; and &quot;not contracting&quot; would definitely be the two. It's certainly way easier than for water to flow against gravity or for electricity to move against the way of the least resistance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12892-kammerer","name":"Kammerer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12892_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-30T13:14:01-07:00","id":1098527,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kammerer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1097992-fighting-with-2-dot-arcana?p=1098523#post1098523\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can you combine Control Heat (Forces 2) with Life 2 to cook someone alive by raising their temperature by ten grades or so?</div> </div> </div> </div>You wouldn't need Life for this.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kammerer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1097992-fighting-with-2-dot-arcana?p=1098524#post1098524\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Uh. All living organisms can do that? Heart is a muscle, and <i>not </i>contracting is pretty easy. If muscles had &quot;fundamental abilities&quot;, then &quot;contracting&quot; and &quot;not contracting&quot; would definitely be the two. It's certainly way easier than for water to flow against gravity or for electricity to move against the way of the least resistance.</div> </div> </div> </div>We'll have to agree to disagree. Scientifically, sure the 'heart' is a muscle. Looking at it from a more symbolic perspective (the perspective magic operates on) it's an entirely different beast, and altering the thing that universally keeps a living thing living to make it stop doing so would be a fundamental alteration of abilities at my table.<br /> <br /> Implying that all living organisms can stop their heart from beating because the brief moment between beats when they're not contracting is <i>technically</i> normal functionality is the kind of rationale that we'd disregard entirely.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-30T13:16:33-07:00","id":1098528,"title":"","content":"How would you feel about causing your heart to beat too fast or too slow, or to stop blood in your veins from moving? I have hard time &quot;grokking&quot; Ruling, as making water flow uphill and ignore gravity throws me a curve ball.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-30T13:18:10-07:00","id":1098529,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kammerer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1097992-fighting-with-2-dot-arcana?p=1098523#post1098523\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can you combine Control Heat (Forces 2) with Life 2 to cook someone alive by raising their temperature by ten grades or so?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Temperature manipulation is my go-to tactic against Mages and other supernaturals, as Extreme Environments cause pretty massive penalties to all rolls (and I assume all includes supernatural and magic) on top of doing DoT style per turn damage. It's also easy to insulate yourself against it, so it's a nice &quot;nuke all&quot; panic button.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-30T13:19:41-07:00","id":1098531,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1097992-fighting-with-2-dot-arcana?p=1098527#post1098527\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We'll have to agree to disagree. Scientifically, sure the 'heart' is a muscle. Looking at it from a more symbolic perspective (the perspective magic operates on) it's an entirely different beast, and altering the thing that universally keeps a living thing living to make it stop doing so would be a fundamental alteration of abilities at my table.<br /> <br /> Implying that all living organisms can stop their heart from beating because the brief moment between beats when they're not contracting is <i>technically</i> normal functionality is the kind of rationale that we'd disregard entirely.</div> </div> </div> </div>Your idea of Ruling is incoherent. Making the heart stop is not a fundamental alteration of abilties. &quot;Not beating&quot; is an ability heart already has. You are just forcing it to use this ability.<br /> <br /> If anything it's Mutable Mask that doesn't fit in the Ruling.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> She can change skin pigments, phenotypical features, apparent sex, or hair color and texture; add or subtract small fat deposits; or change the sound of the subject\u2019s voice. Distinguishing features like scars and moles can be added or removed. </div> </div> </div>Any and all of these are way more extreme than contracting a muscle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12892-kammerer","name":"Kammerer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12892_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-30T13:22:49-07:00","id":1098534,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1097992-fighting-with-2-dot-arcana?p=1098529#post1098529\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Temperature manipulation is my go-to tactic against Mages and other supernaturals, as Extreme Environments cause pretty massive penalties to all rolls (and I assume all includes supernatural and magic) on top of doing DoT style per turn damage. It's also easy to insulate yourself against it, so it's a nice &quot;nuke all&quot; panic button.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, I mean literally heat up target's body by ten grades. Proteins in blood start to cook at about 43 celcius, and you should be able to push it way above that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12892-kammerer","name":"Kammerer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12892_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-30T13:27:30-07:00","id":1098535,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1097992-fighting-with-2-dot-arcana?p=1098528#post1098528\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How would you feel about causing your heart to beat too fast or too slow, or to stop blood in your veins from moving?</div> </div> </div> </div>This definitely seems doable - hearts can fundamentally beat faster or slower, it's part of what they do.<br /> <br /> Make the heart rush so fast it gives out, or slow down so much that the victim loses consciousness and eventually dies as no blood reaches their brain? Brutal but definitely Ruling as I see it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1097992-fighting-with-2-dot-arcana?p=1098528#post1098528\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have hard time &quot;grokking&quot; Ruling, as making water flow uphill and ignore gravity throws me a curve ball.</div> </div> </div> </div>It comes down to what you consider a<i> fundamental ability</i> of the subject. <s>Water will flow uphill under the right circumstances (high pressure behind it). Does that mean forcing water to flow uphill without that pressure is still within it's fundamental abilities? Per RAW, I guess so. Water can also be forced to turn solid or gaseous under the right circumstances, but altering that is apparently altering a fundamental ability.</s> See the way Ashenrogue addressed this below, it makes more sense.<br /> <br /> I've found the more I design spells the more I <i>think</i> I understand how it's all supposed to work, but it's almost impossible to actually put into words and I probably butcher half my spells in the end, anyway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3570,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","user":"lnodiv","date":". 05-30-2017, 04:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-30T13:30:22-07:00","id":1098536,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1097992-fighting-with-2-dot-arcana?p=1098528#post1098528\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How would you feel about causing your heart to beat too fast or too slow, or to stop blood in your veins from moving? I have hard time &quot;grokking&quot; Ruling, as making water flow uphill and ignore gravity throws me a curve ball.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd let that work. Using symbolic logic, a heart is something that beats. It beats at different rates depending on the situation, but if it functions as it's supposed to it is going to beat. The rate, however, is something you could almost certainly fuck around with. It is still beating, still fulfilling its symbolic purpose, but it happens to be doing so in such a way that screws up everything around it.<br /> <br /> The logic for water flowing uphill and the like is that symbolically, water flows. That's what it does. It flows until it can't flow anymore then it pools. Now normally it only really has permission to flow downwards, led around by gravity and the like, but using magic you can grant it permission to flow elsewhere. It still has to be able to flow, or pool if it is unable to do that, but the limitation of <i>where</i> it is allowed to do so can be made less restrictive.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-30T13:32:02-07:00","id":1098537,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Your idea of Ruling is incoherent. </div> </div> </div>Tone down the hostility, please.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> &quot;Not beating&quot; is an ability heart already has. </div> </div> </div>I disagree. Ashenrogue has the right idea:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ashenrogue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1097992-fighting-with-2-dot-arcana?p=1098536#post1098536\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Using symbolic logic, a heart is something that beats. It beats at different rates depending on the situation, but if it functions as it's supposed to it is going to beat. The rate, however, is something you could almost certainly fuck around with. It is still beating, still fulfilling its symbolic purpose, but it happens to be doing so in such a way that screws up everything around it.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kammerer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1097992-fighting-with-2-dot-arcana?p=1098531#post1098531\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If anything it's Mutable Mask that doesn't fit in the Ruling.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's because it's Veiling...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-30T13:32:57-07:00","id":1098538,"title":"","content":"So would that allow Life to make people walk in the air using a Ruling spell, as long as they are doing the physical motions of moving/climbing?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-30T13:44:28-07:00","id":1098543,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1097992-fighting-with-2-dot-arcana?p=1098537#post1098537\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Tone down the hostility, please.</div> </div> </div> </div>Tone down the ego and don't treat everything like a personal attack on yourself, please. Practice of Ruling provides a few examples of what is considered to be commanding without fundamental alteration. You can move around water, you can twist matter, you can command animals, you can slow down or speed up time. It further clarifies what Ruling isn't. Ruling can't change its targets. You can't control water, but you can't turn it into gas. You can control time, but not change it. You can control animal, but not make it a different animal. And by that logic stopping a heart is absolutely ruling because you don't change the heart. You command it to stop. You don't turn heart into liver or something. This is the exact same effect as moving around water.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1097992-fighting-with-2-dot-arcana?p=1098537#post1098537\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's because it's Veiling...</div> </div> </div> </div>It fits in Veiling even less because changing how you look has nothing to do with Veiling. Veiling hides the subject under its purview, or hides the things in arcana's purview from the subject. Changing your skin color is neither and by all rights should be Weaving. In fact, it is Weaving! At Life 3, &quot;Many Faces&quot;. I genuinely don't understand what &quot;the changes brough on by this spell are illusionary&quot; means. Why is this Veiling? Why does it affect biometric scanners - they are not in the purview of Life. Why is there a limitation against mimicing specific people? That seems incredibly arbitrary.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12892,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12892-kammerer","user":"Kammerer","date":". 05-30-2017, 04:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12892-kammerer","name":"Kammerer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12892_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-30T13:45:46-07:00","id":1098544,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1097992-fighting-with-2-dot-arcana?p=1098538#post1098538\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So would that allow Life to make people walk in the air using a Ruling spell, as long as they are doing the physical motions of moving/climbing?</div> </div> </div> </div>I guess that depends on whether you believe walking is symbolically part of what a human is, which I don't quite think is true. Walking is something humans can do, but it isn't some inherent quality of humans. Again, speaking purely symbolically, walking would be a separate modifier that can and often is applied to humans but isn't part of them in and of itself (this is one of those things where people, and animals are kinda complicated).<br /> <br /> So the act of flowing, at least in my mind, is inherent in water, and matter can mess around with the inherent properties of water. Walking to me is more an aspect of Space. It is a means of traversing perceived distance in order to sympathetically become closer to something and/or further from something else. That said, like most symbolic things it could be argued otherwise.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-30T13:52:18-07:00","id":1098549,"title":"","content":"It seems to be a general problem with mage where they want some spells to be certain level, but that doesn't fit into the system of practices they made. Example: Animal Minion (Life 4). Practice of Patterning. You take over a body and puppeteer it. It definitely seems like Ruling effect to me, since Patterning is about transformations.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Patterning spells allow a mage to completely transform a target into something else that falls under the Arcanum\u2019s purview. A memory can be replaced wholesale (Mind), the mage can turn herself (or a target) into an animal (Life), or she can teleport by \u201crewriting\u201d her own location (Space). A spell that transforms the target into something that falls within the Purview of another Arcanum, like transforming into a living pillar of fire (Life and Forces), requires a mage to know the Practice of Patterning for the destination Arcanum. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12892-kammerer","name":"Kammerer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12892_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-30T13:55:43-07:00","id":1098554,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kammerer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1097992-fighting-with-2-dot-arcana?p=1098543#post1098543\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">don't treat everything like a personal attack on yourself, please.</div> </div> </div> </div>That'd be a lot easier if you didn't call my ideas incoherent. There aren't many ways to take that that aren't a personal attack.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kammerer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1097992-fighting-with-2-dot-arcana?p=1098543#post1098543\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You command it to stop....This is the exact same effect as moving around water.</div> </div> </div> </div>From my perspective, the symbolic differences between stopping a thing <i>whose sole purpose </i>is to beat from beating and adjusting the direction that the thing that flows, flows, are not at all similar.<br /> <br /> I get that you disagree. We have fundamentally incompatible perspectives. This discussion is not going to go anywhere.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kammerer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1097992-fighting-with-2-dot-arcana?p=1098543#post1098543\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It fits in Veiling even less because changing how you look has nothing to do with Veiling. Veiling hides the subject under its purview, or hides the things in arcana's purview from the subject. Changing your skin color is neither and by all rights should be Weaving. In fact, it is Weaving! At Life 3, &quot;Many Faces&quot;. I genuinely don't understand what &quot;the changes brough on by this spell are illusionary&quot; means. Why is this Veiling? Why does it affect biometric scanners - they are not in the purview of Life.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Magically disguise me to make me look like not-me&quot; falls under the Practice of Veiling so perfectly that it's really hard to think of something that fits it <i>better. </i><br /> <br /> You're shielding something under the purview of the Arcanum (a living being) from detection (via a disguise). It works on biometrics because that's another form of detection, and it's about shielding something under the arcanum <i>from</i> detection, so the scanners don't have to be under the purview, because the subject is.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kammerer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1097992-fighting-with-2-dot-arcana?p=1098543#post1098543\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why is there a limitation against mimicing specific people? That seems incredibly arbitrary.</div> </div> </div> </div>It does. I'd guess because the point of the spell isn't &quot;Make me look like that guy&quot; it's &quot;Veil my true appearance.&quot; The two concepts are related, however, so the former is achievable via Reach.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kammerer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1097992-fighting-with-2-dot-arcana?p=1098549#post1098549\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It seems to be a general problem with mage where they want some spells to be certain level, but that doesn't fit into the system of practices they made. Example: Animal Minion (Life 4). Practice of Patterning. You take over a body and puppeteer it. It definitely seems like Ruling effect to me, since Patterning is about transformations.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I don't understand why this is Patterning at all. Everything about it says Ruling to me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3570,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","user":"lnodiv","date":". 05-30-2017, 05:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-30T14:28:11-07:00","id":1098564,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1097992-fighting-with-2-dot-arcana?p=1098554#post1098554\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, I don't understand why this is Patterning at all. Everything about it says Ruling to me.</div> </div> </div> </div>Note that Psychic Domination's status as Ruling is predicated on the idea that you're planting overriding commands in a subject's mind in much the same way as Control Instincts runs on the concept of pulling the right neurological strings. Animal Minion is almost explicitly a Life-based version of Possession \u2014 you're not telling the subject what to do, you've <i>written yourself into the driver's seat of their body</i>. Despite how the Creative Thaum breakdown is phrased, Patterning has never been purely about transformations in the prosaic sense of &quot;turn a thing into a different thing.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-30T14:31:01-07:00","id":1098567,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1097992-fighting-with-2-dot-arcana?p=1098564#post1098564\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Despite how the Creative Thaum breakdown is phrased, Patterning has never been purely about transformations in the prosaic sense of &quot;turn a thing into a different thing.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>How can anyone possibly know that when Patterning only ever talks about turning a thing into a different thing?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12892-kammerer","name":"Kammerer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12892_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-30T14:50:44-07:00","id":1098569,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1097992-fighting-with-2-dot-arcana?p=1098520#post1098520\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But Life, for some reason, has this type of effect at Life 4.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Life 4 version moves you into your subject's body, it's basically the Life version of Possession, and that's why it's at Life 4. Life 2 should be able to exert gross physical control like Psychic Domination.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-30T14:53:54-07:00","id":1098571,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kammerer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1097992-fighting-with-2-dot-arcana?p=1098531#post1098531\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If anything it's Mutable Mask that doesn't fit in the Ruling.</div> </div> </div> </div>That spell is Veiling, not Ruling, all the changes are purely illusory so it makes perfect sense.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-30T14:59:40-07:00","id":1098573,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kammerer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1097992-fighting-with-2-dot-arcana?p=1098567#post1098567\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How can anyone possibly know that when Patterning only ever talks about turning a thing into a different thing?</div> </div> </div> </div>You're turning yourself into the driver of another being's body. Obviously.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-30T16:08:11-07:00","id":1098599,"title":"","content":"Ah, that sweet moment when magic doesn't work like it's supposed to, with &quot;supposed to&quot; meaning &quot;what (modern human understanding of) the laws of physics say.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-30T16:19:44-07:00","id":1098604,"title":"","content":"Overall, the magic system is pretty coherent if you pay attention to what the example spells are actually doing.<br /> <br /> That whole tangent doesn't really address what the OP is getting at though. So in the spirit of getting back on track, yes, 2 dots in an arcana can have pretty lethal consequences, but those consequences aren't likely to be spelled out in direct translations of casting a spell and doing a set X amount of damage. It's likely to be less direct, but it has a decent chance of being -more- lethal as a result if you can follow the logic for what the arcana and practices do.<br /> <br /> Other examples, any of the ephemeral entities can be forced to come into contact with their Bane via their corresponding arcana, or they can be forced to fight on your behalf.<br /> <br /> Fate and Time take perhaps the least direct routes, but you can enhance your spell-casting or combat skills significantly while also minimizing the chances of being caught unprepared in an encounter.<br /> <br /> Prime probably isn't the best combat arcana at only 2 dots.<br /> <br /> Space also isn't that great, except that you can target your enemies via Sympathy and skip out on the part of conflicts that tend to be face to face. Matter, Life, Mind and Forces are probably the most in your face and can be devastating pretty quick.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2632,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","user":"Mrmdubois","date":". 05-30-2017, 07:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-31T00:12:38-07:00","id":1098679,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kammerer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1097992-fighting-with-2-dot-arcana?p=1098543#post1098543\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Tone down the ego and don't treat everything like a personal attack on yourself, please.</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">\u200bPlease don't tell someone to tone down the ego when they tell you something is coming across like a personal attack. The correct response would have been to apologize and state it wasn't meant to come across as such and then move on with the conversation. This was needlessly hostile, don't do it again.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Onyx Path Forum Administrator</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">Posts in this color are moderator posts</span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\"><span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this color mean a Great Old One has driven me mad.</span></span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","name":"Darksider","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11_2.jpeg","title":"Forum Administrator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1692"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-31T15:18:17-07:00","id":1098915,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ashenrogue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1097992-fighting-with-2-dot-arcana?p=1098536#post1098536\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd let that work. Using symbolic logic, a heart is something that beats. It beats at different rates depending on the situation, but if it functions as it's supposed to it is going to beat. The rate, however, is something you could almost certainly fuck around with. It is still beating, still fulfilling its symbolic purpose, but it happens to be doing so in such a way that screws up everything around it.<br /> .</div> </div> </div> </div>So, Slowing the heart down to a beting rythm of 1 beat per hour works for you then? Still fulfilling its fundamental ability, but the organism linked to that heartbeat dies between the beats. This is fundamentally no different than just stopping the contraction of the hearty completely. Either way, the target is dead. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">The problem with defending the purity of the English language is that English is about as pure as a cribhouse whore. We don't just borrow words; on occasion, English has pursued other languages down alleyways to beat them unconscious and rifle their pockets for new vocabulary. - James. D. Nicoll</span></span></i>","edited":{"userid":540,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","user":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","date":". 05-31-2017, 06:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","name":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-31T18:28:03-07:00","id":1098953,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tymeaus Jalynsfein</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1097992-fighting-with-2-dot-arcana?p=1098915#post1098915\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So, Slowing the heart down to a beting rythm of 1 beat per hour works for you then? Still fulfilling its fundamental ability, but the organism linked to that heartbeat dies between the beats. This is fundamentally no different than just stopping the contraction of the hearty completely. Either way, the target is dead. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>That's literally the purview of Unmaking.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-31T19:26:14-07:00","id":1098987,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tymeaus Jalynsfein</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1097992-fighting-with-2-dot-arcana?p=1098915#post1098915\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So, Slowing the heart down to a beting rythm of 1 beat per hour works for you then? Still fulfilling its fundamental ability, but the organism linked to that heartbeat dies between the beats. This is fundamentally no different than just stopping the contraction of the hearty completely. Either way, the target is dead. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> By &quot;fundamentally no different&quot; you are saying &quot;not different in the laws of physics.&quot;<br /> <br /> A heart that is only technically beating and unable to sustain a living being is not, symbolically speaking, a beating heart.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-01T01:50:15-07:00","id":1099074,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I wouldn't allow Ruling to slow a heartbeat to the point that it could kill a subject. It could induce lethargy though from poor circulation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-01T02:58:45-07:00","id":1099086,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tymeaus Jalynsfein</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1097992-fighting-with-2-dot-arcana?p=1098915#post1098915\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So, Slowing the heart down to a beting rythm of 1 beat per hour works for you then? Still fulfilling its fundamental ability, but the organism linked to that heartbeat dies between the beats. This is fundamentally no different than just stopping the contraction of the hearty completely. Either way, the target is dead. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Magic isn't about the final result, it's about how you get there.<br /> <br /> This is why using Psychic Domination to force someone to kill themselves works, but a Mind 2 spell that just erases their mind doesn't. One of them is within the capabilities of Ruling, the other is Unmaking.<br /> <br /> As for slowing the heart so much that it's only beating once a minute, essentially ensuring death? With enough Potency, sure. If you aren't going to actually try to incorporate Spell Factors into Creative Thaumaturgy you can make anything sound ridiculous by assuming any technically-possible effect can achieve the maximum possible result consistently.<br /> <br /> &quot;Causing an earthquake is within the capabilities of Matter 2.&quot;<br /> &quot;So you're okay if someone levels an entire city with it???&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-01T03:44:51-07:00","id":1099093,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tymeaus Jalynsfein</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1097992-fighting-with-2-dot-arcana?p=1098915#post1098915\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So, Slowing the heart down to a beting rythm of 1 beat per hour works for you then? Still fulfilling its fundamental ability, but the organism linked to that heartbeat dies between the beats. This is fundamentally no different than just stopping the contraction of the hearty completely. Either way, the target is dead. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Yep, slowing it way down is fine imo, even if that rate is enough to kill the target. And there's a pretty big difference symbolically. It's as Inodiv said, it isn't the final result that magic cares about, but how you go about it specifically, And while you can almost certainly do it, it probably won't be <i>that</i> easy to pull off. I'd assume such a spell would be something like half the rate at which someones heart beats per point of Potency. It'd only take around 3-4 points of Potency to become a major problem in a short amount of time, but it'd still be something you'd need to dedicate at least a little effort towards.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-01T04:27:49-07:00","id":1099110,"title":"","content":"So just like Psychic Domination, another Ruling spell that requires hefty Reach to pull off suicidal commands, I'd say that this heart-slowing spell we talk about normally can't kill somebody, but can with enough Reach.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-01T08:07:19-07:00","id":1099153,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1097992-fighting-with-2-dot-arcana?p=1099086#post1099086\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Magic isn't about the final result, it's about how you get there.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually magic in Awakening is all about the end result. That's how Imagos work, you picture the result, magic fills the gaps if it's within your skill.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-01T08:46:12-07:00","id":1099164,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thorbes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1097992-fighting-with-2-dot-arcana?p=1099153#post1099153\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually magic in Awakening is all about the end result. That's how Imagos work, you picture the result, magic fills the gaps if it's within your skill.</div> </div> </div> </div>The way that's used in the book, to refer to the creation of Imagos, and the way it's being used in this conversation are completely different. This is obvious by paying attention to the spells that actually exist.<br /> <br /> In Practice (capitalization intended) it's not about the narrative 'end result', it's about what the 'end result' is when the magic stops and natural consequences take hold.<br /> <br /> Is the 'end result' someone's heart slowing down super far? From the perspective of an Imago, yes. The magic stops there. The natural consequences are what lead to the true 'end result' of death (what we're actually talking about).<br /> <br /> It is, again, the same reason you can kill someone with Mind 2 without Unmaking, Or Space 3 by Banning the oxygen around them. The 'end result' is death in both cases, but how you get there is what matters, and what determines the Practice (because the Practice informs where the magic stops). If how you got there didn't matter, it would be literally impossible to ever kill anyone via magic in any way below 5 dots in the Arcanum, which is demonstrably untrue.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3570,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","user":"lnodiv","date":". 06-01-2017, 11:49 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-01T18:05:36-07:00","id":1099343,"title":"","content":"I have to imagine you could fight using Life 2 and focusing on the microflora of someone's guts (especially if you can &quot;prep&quot; the person). Sure, might not kill them, but when you're having a sudden case of needing a bathroom in the middle of danger... well, there's a reason why sound weapons were a concept.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr />\u200bWhen noise turns to silence, when colors dull and pale, when reality no longer makes sense, there shall you find me. There, in the dreams of the River of Faceless Millions, do I dwell.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/\" target=\"_blank\">http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/</a> for my art.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/378-haren","name":"haren","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar378_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"664"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-01T18:55:31-07:00","id":1099354,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>haren</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1097992-fighting-with-2-dot-arcana?p=1099343#post1099343\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have to imagine you could fight using Life 2 and focusing on the microflora of someone's guts (especially if you can &quot;prep&quot; the person). Sure, might not kill them, but when you're having a sudden case of needing a bathroom in the middle of danger... well, there's a reason why sound weapons were a concept.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm pretty sure you can't do that as there's no possible way you'd have line of sight with someone's gut microflora.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12892-kammerer","name":"Kammerer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12892_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-01T19:02:28-07:00","id":1099356,"title":"","content":"I'm pretty sure the microflora is considered a part of a person for the purposes of spell targetting, so you only need to target the human for the spell to be able to affect the microflora.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-02T00:23:00-07:00","id":1099406,"title":"","content":"You don't even need to target the microflora specifically.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-02T01:27:06-07:00","id":1099410,"title":"","content":"Good point <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2632\" data-vbnamecard=\"2632\">Mrmdubois</a>, but when you went to school for Microbiology, it's the hammer and everything looks like nails problem.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr />\u200bWhen noise turns to silence, when colors dull and pale, when reality no longer makes sense, there shall you find me. There, in the dreams of the River of Faceless Millions, do I dwell.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/\" target=\"_blank\">http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/</a> for my art.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/378-haren","name":"haren","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar378_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"664"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-02T10:39:28-07:00","id":1099569,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1097992-fighting-with-2-dot-arcana?p=1099356#post1099356\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm pretty sure the microflora is considered a part of a person for the purposes of spell targetting, so you only need to target the human for the spell to be able to affect the microflora.</div> </div> </div> </div>Right, I don't need to see a brain scan to affect their behavior with Mind or Life.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-02T10:45:16-07:00","id":1099573,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kammerer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1097992-fighting-with-2-dot-arcana?p=1099354#post1099354\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm pretty sure you can't do that as there's no possible way you'd have line of sight with someone's gut microflora.</div> </div> </div> </div>Line of sight isn't really a thing in Mage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}